## Goal
Run the local Vite frontend (`/home/alexlee/dev/EnderAI-frontend`) against the Render-hosted FastAPI backend.

## Ground Truth Pointers
- Frontend sets API base via `VITE_API_URL`: `/home/alexlee/dev/EnderAI-frontend/.env` and `/home/alexlee/dev/EnderAI-frontend/src/main.tsx`.
- Backend CORS config lives in:
  - `demo/full-stack-fastapi-template/backend/app/main.py` (CORSMiddleware wiring)
  - `demo/full-stack-fastapi-template/backend/app/core/config.py` (`FRONTEND_HOST`, `BACKEND_CORS_ORIGINS`, `all_cors_origins`)

## Local Frontend -> Remote Backend Setup
1) Set local frontend env:
   - Create `/home/alexlee/dev/EnderAI-frontend/.env.local` with:
     - `VITE_API_URL=https://<render-backend-origin>`
2) Ensure backend allows local dev origin in CORS:
   - Current (from user):
     - `FRONTEND_HOST=https://al-exe.github.io`
     - `BACKEND_CORS_ORIGINS=https://al-exe.github.io,https://al-exe.github.io/EnderAI-frontend`
   - Update to include local Vite dev origin:
     - `BACKEND_CORS_ORIGINS=https://al-exe.github.io,https://al-exe.github.io/EnderAI-frontend,http://localhost:5173`
3) Run frontend:
   - `bun install`
   - `bun run dev`

## Notes
- Prefer token auth for cross-origin local dev (already used by frontend via `OpenAPI.TOKEN` reading localStorage).
- Do not store secrets (DB creds, tokens) in repo docs/logs; use env vars and redact values.
